  "notes": [
    "Weapon definitions. sim.js reads ONLY this file for weapon behaviour; add a weapon by adding an entry, not code.",
    "fire: 'hitscan' (instant rays, `pellets` per shot for shotguns), 'projectile' (thrown/launched, explodes), 'melee'.",
    "Angles are radians. Spread is the gaussian sigma of the aim error per ray. Distances are metres, times seconds.",
    "Hitboxes: body cylinder r=0.42 h=1.42, head sphere r=0.25 at 1.62 (sim.js BODY). Headshot = damage.head.",
    "TTK sanity: body hits to kill = ceil(100 / damage.body). Keep ARs at 4-5, SMGs 5-6 at their faster interval.",
    "Balance check: `node tools/botsim.mjs weapons <map>` (6 seeds of 6v6, all-Karens). Aim for every primary inside 0.75-1.35 K/D on culdesac, stripmall AND pickleball; a step change in falloff (`mult`) is a cliff for players, so tune `startM` first.",
    "MEASURE WITH A BIG SAMPLE: `node tools/botsim.mjs weapons <map> --seeds=20`. Six seeds is noise - the sniper read 1.68 on pickleball then 1.13 on the next run with no AR change in between, and tuning against that chases luck. The tool now prints a 1-sigma error on every K/D.",
    "Measured 2024-06-20 seeds, all-Karen teams: culdesac 0.89-1.16, stripmall 0.87-1.10, pickleball 0.73-1.41 (every primary inside 0.75-1.35 except the two role cases below).",
    "Two readings outside the band are deliberate. Pickleball's sniper (1.41+-0.16) wins by NOT dying - long open courts, it never has to cross no-man's land, so K/D overstates its power; that is the map favouring a role, and cutting it further made it a trap on culdesac (0.87). The shotgun (0.73+-0.05 on pickleball, 0.94 on culdesac) is the same story in reverse: a 19 m falloff on a 60 m court. Both are role/map fits, not outliers to chase - check that a buff does not push them out of band on the maps where they already sit at 0.9+.",
    "The 8 launch weapons from the GDD: allowance (AR), sideHustle (SMG), divorceSettlement (shotgun), trustFund (sniper), subdivision (LMG), permit (pistol), lawsuit (launcher; thrown briefcase), participationTrophy (melee)."
